  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1216 AM MDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nCurrently, showers and isolated thunderstorms are tapering off,\nespecially west of the RGV. This has been the trend in the CAMs\nand have tapered NBM PoPs down for this afternoon and evening. \nThere is still some potential for convective development this \nafternoon over the east as there are still some disturbances \nmoving through. These have the potential to produce very heavy \nrainfall in an almost tropical environment. Then, the HRRR and \neven the GFS are showing a SW-NE band of thunderstorms developing \nnear El Paso along an inverted surface trough. Kept PoPs going \nthere higher than other areas after midnight. \n\nAs we move into Thu, through the morning it just looks like some\nlingering showers east, but then we get some convectively induced\ndisturbances moving up out of Mexico in the aftn/evening which\nwill bring another round of storms to the entire CWA. There is\nsome modest instability around of 500-1000J/kg CAPE and moisture\nremains above normal so heavy rain will again be the main threat.\nTemperatures will struggle out east to get above the lower to mid \n70s while areas out west where I'm expecting at least some sun \nwill get to around 80.\n\nFor Fri, the upper trough that has been lingering off to the west\nwill lift out and the main axis will be east of the area by 00Z\nSat. Isolated to widely scattered storms are possible with the\ntrough passage and again decent CAPE but with mid-upper level \ndrying and some shear so may need to be aware of severe. Temperatures\nwill warm areawide with lower to mid 80s for the lowlands and did\nraise NBM temps a few degrees.\n\n\nThe dry air is fully entrenched for Saturday with the influence of\nthe next trough moving into the west for later Sunday. A few\nstorms are possible here, but we will have to really watch if the\nremnants of Polo move up this way. GFS is much more aggressive\nwith this moisture getting caught up in the next trough than the\nEC.  This would be a heavy rain maker again if it does happen.",
